<div class="help-home" data-help-start><div class="help-home-heading"><h2>What would you like to do?</h2><span data-help-results role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div><nav class="help-grid" aria-label="Help topics"><button type="button" class="help-card" data-help-open="projectUserGuideContent-task-find" aria-controls="projectUserGuideContent-task-find" aria-expanded="false"><span class="help-card-icon"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="m16 16 5 5"/></svg></span><span class="help-card-copy"><strong>Find a project</strong><small>Search, filters and your dashboard.</small></span><span class="help-card-arrow"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></button><button type="button" class="help-card" data-help-open="projectUserGuideContent-task-edit" aria-controls="projectUserGuideContent-task-edit" aria-expanded="false"><span class="help-card-icon"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m16 3 5 5M4 20l4-1L21 6a2 2 0 0 0-5-3L3 16l-1 5Z"/></svg></span><span class="help-card-copy"><strong>Add or edit a project</strong><small>Save changes and attach files.</small></span><span class="help-card-arrow"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></button><button type="button" class="help-card" data-help-open="projectUserGuideContent-task-dates" aria-controls="projectUserGuideContent-task-dates" aria-expanded="false"><span class="help-card-icon"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M16 3v4M8 3v4M3 11h18M8 15h2M14 15h2"/></svg></span><span class="help-card-copy"><strong>Dates &amp; reminders</strong><small>Deadlines, status and resolved alerts.</small></span><span class="help-card-arrow"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></button><button type="button" class="help-card" data-help-open="projectUserGuideContent-task-files" aria-controls="projectUserGuideContent-task-files" aria-expanded="false"><span class="help-card-icon"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8ZM14 2v6h6M8 13h8M8 17h5"/></svg></span><span class="help-card-copy"><strong>Import, export &amp; print</strong><small>Spreadsheets, printing and archives.</small></span><span class="help-card-arrow"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></button><button type="button" class="help-card" data-help-open="projectUserGuideContent-task-deletion" aria-controls="projectUserGuideContent-task-deletion" aria-expanded="false"><span class="help-card-icon"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6h18M9 6V3h6v3M5 6l1 15h12l1-15M10 10v7M14 10v7"/></svg></span><span class="help-card-copy"><strong>Delete &amp; clear history</strong><small>Requests, approvals and personal history.</small></span><span class="help-card-arrow"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></button><button type="button" class="help-card" data-help-open="projectUserGuideContent-task-account" aria-controls="projectUserGuideContent-task-account" aria-expanded="false"><span class="help-card-icon"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="4"/><path d="M4 21v-2a8 8 0 0 1 16 0v2"/></svg></span><span class="help-card-copy"><strong>Your account &amp; settings</strong><small>Profile, access and office settings.</small></span><span class="help-card-arrow"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></button></nav><div class="help-empty" data-help-empty hidden><strong>No matching topics</strong><p>Try a different word, or clear the search to see all topics.</p><button type="button" class="help-reset-search" data-help-clear>Show all topics</button></div></div>
<section id="projectUserGuideContent-task-find" class="help-task" data-help-task hidden aria-labelledby="projectUserGuideContent-task-find-title"><button type="button" class="help-back" data-help-home><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m14 5-7 7 7 7"/></svg><span>All topics</span></button><h2 id="projectUserGuideContent-task-find-title" tabindex="-1">Find a project</h2><p class="help-task-description">Search, filters and your dashboard.</p><ol class="help-steps"><li>Open <strong>View All Projects</strong> from the sidebar.</li><li>Search by project name or number, or use the filters.</li><li>Select a project title to see its details and alerts.</li></ol><p class="help-note">Clear your filters if a project seems to be missing.</p><div class="help-more"><h3>More details</h3><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-2" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-2-title">Dashboard and notifications</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><ol>
        <li>The <strong>Total Projects, Pending</strong> and <strong>Active Alerts</strong> cards open their corresponding project views. Counts cover non-archived projects. Use the status chart’s month/year filters and Monthly Completions’ year filter to explore the registry.</li>
        <li><strong>Recently updated projects</strong> shows saved changes. <strong>Needs attention</strong> groups alerts by project; search and use Previous/Next to review additional pages.</li>
        <li>Select a project title for its details, or <strong>Alerts</strong> for individual reminders, deadlines and resolution dates. The notification bell works on every page. Selecting a project or its Alerts button closes Notifications and opens that project.</li>
    </ol></div></details><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-3" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-3-title">Search, filters and project details</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><ol>
        <li>In <strong>View All Projects</strong>, choose <strong>Active projects, Completed projects, Released projects, Active alerts</strong> or <strong>All projects</strong>. Archived records are in <strong>Historical Archive</strong>.</li>
        <li>Search records and combine the status, exact project number, barangay and selected milestone date filters. Select a date field, then its month, day or year as needed. Clear filters when a record is missing from your results.</li>
        <li>Select the project-number heading to reverse the sort order. Use pagination for more results. Select a title to open <strong>Project Details</strong>, including financial information, dates, remarks, attachments and Alerts.</li>
        <li>Use the row’s <strong>Logs</strong> button to review saved edits and timeline actions in the project’s <strong>Audit Trail</strong>. Each entry shows when the change was saved and the user who made it; older entries without a recorded user show <strong>Not recorded</strong>. Use <strong>Print</strong> to open the formatted summary, then your browser’s print or Save as PDF option. Printed summaries are reference copies.</li>
    </ol></div></details></div></section><section id="projectUserGuideContent-task-edit" class="help-task" data-help-task hidden aria-labelledby="projectUserGuideContent-task-edit-title"><button type="button" class="help-back" data-help-home><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m14 5-7 7 7 7"/></svg><span>All topics</span></button><h2 id="projectUserGuideContent-task-edit-title" tabindex="-1">Add or edit a project</h2><p class="help-task-description">Save changes and attach files.</p><ol class="help-steps"><li>Choose <strong>Add Project</strong>, or open a project and select <strong>Edit</strong>.</li><li>Enter the details and add any files you need.</li><li>Select <strong>Save Project</strong> or <strong>Apply Records Change</strong>, then wait for confirmation.</li></ol><p class="help-note">If a record changed while you were editing, review the latest version before saving again.</p><div class="help-more"><h3>More details</h3><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-4" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-4-title">Add and edit project records</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><ol>
        <li>Choose <strong>Add Project</strong>. Enter the required <strong>Project Title</strong> and <strong>Approved Budget for the Contract</strong>. Include the location in the title, for example “Residential Building at Brgy. 1”. Add the bidding date and winning bidder when available. The next project number is a preview; the server confirms the assigned number when saving.</li>
        <li>Complete the relevant sections: project information and fund source (use <strong>Others</strong> for a custom source); bidding and bid amount; bidder; purchase request and obligation dates; resolution; post qualification; NOA deadline and issuance; performance bond; contract date and duration; NTP; DOLE clearance; inspection, testing, SWA and completion; liquidated damages; and remarks.</li>
        <li>Enter amounts as non-negative numbers with at most two decimal places. Enter <strong>Contract Duration</strong> as a positive number of working days, such as <strong>30</strong> or <strong>30.5</strong>. Do not append “days”. The Contract Due Date is calculated from the Contract Date and duration. Liquidated-damages fields record the amount, number of days, revised completion date and actual duration; entering a revised date does not replace the calculated contract deadline.</li>
        <li>Select <strong>Save Project</strong> and wait for confirmation. To update a project, use its <strong>Edit</strong> action, review the fields and choose <strong>Apply Records Change</strong>. <strong>Cancel</strong> or the editor’s close button discards unsaved edits.</li>
        <li>The save button shows <strong>Saving</strong> while the request is in progress. A successful save shows a brief confirmation, and the header message clears. <strong>Save failed</strong> remains visible and leaves your draft open for correction. Only a successful server response confirms saving. If saving succeeds but the view update fails, the notification distinguishes the saved record from the pending refresh.</li>
    </ol></div></details><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-8" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-8-title">Attachments</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><ol>
        <li>Save a new project first, then edit it to add attachments. Choose files and use <strong>Add</strong>. PDF, Word, Excel, text and image files are supported, up to <strong>25 MB each</strong> and <strong>20 uploaded files per save</strong>.</li>
        <li>Added files and removals remain pending until <strong>Apply Records Change</strong> succeeds. A pending attachment draft may be restored in the same browser/account after reopening the page; it has not been uploaded until you save. Cancel discards the draft.</li>
        <li>Select a filename to preview it, or <strong>Download</strong> to save a copy. Preview availability depends on file type/browser support. Editing permission is required to add or remove files.</li>
    </ol></div></details><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-11" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-11-title">Shared updates and simultaneous editing</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><p>Visible tabs check for shared changes about every <strong>3 seconds</strong> and immediately when you return to the tab. Lists, dashboards and open project details update automatically when connected. Hidden/background tabs catch up when you return. Updates wait while you edit or review an import; the <strong>Updates available</strong> button indicates pending changes. Save or cancel your draft to load them safely.</p>
    <p>Two people may edit the same project. The first successful save changes its version; a later stale save is rejected. Your draft remains open. Copy the changes you need, cancel, reopen the latest project and reapply them after reviewing the other person’s work. Changes are not automatically merged.</p>
    <p><strong>Editing indicators</strong> appear below the project title in Project Details and the edit form. They show <strong>No one is editing</strong> when idle, or names and avatars when someone opens <strong>Edit</strong> for that same project. The project list also shows names when editors are active. Viewing Project Details alone does not register you as an editor. They refresh about every <strong>3 seconds</strong>. <strong>Checking editors…</strong> means the initial check is pending; <strong>Editing status unavailable</strong> means the check failed. A successful save, canceling, closing the editor or signing out clears your indicator. An unexpected disconnect or a suspended background tab can take up to <strong>45 seconds</strong> to disappear. The indicator allows simultaneous editing; it does not lock the project, show live typing or share unsaved changes.</p></div></details></div></section><section id="projectUserGuideContent-task-dates" class="help-task" data-help-task hidden aria-labelledby="projectUserGuideContent-task-dates-title"><button type="button" class="help-back" data-help-home><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m14 5-7 7 7 7"/></svg><span>All topics</span></button><h2 id="projectUserGuideContent-task-dates-title" tabindex="-1">Dates &amp; reminders</h2><p class="help-task-description">Deadlines, status and resolved alerts.</p><ol class="help-steps"><li>Open a project’s <strong>Alerts</strong> to check its reminders and due dates.</li><li>After a milestone happens, record its actual date in <strong>Edit</strong> and save.</li><li>Review completed reminders in <strong>Resolved Alerts</strong>.</li></ol><p class="help-note">Completion and SWA should contain actual dates, not planned future dates.</p><div class="help-more"><h3>More details</h3><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-5" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-5-title">Milestone deadlines, actual dates and status</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table table-sm table-bordered">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Milestone</th><th scope="col">Deadline / entry</th><th scope="col">How to resolve</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td data-label="Milestone">Notice of Award (NOA)</td><td data-label="Deadline / entry">Enter <strong>NOA Due Date</strong> separately from the actual <strong>NOA Issued Date</strong>.</td><td data-label="How to resolve">Record the actual issuance date.</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Milestone">Pre-inspection</td><td data-label="Deadline / entry">One calendar month after Bidding Date.</td><td data-label="How to resolve">Record <strong>Pre Inspection</strong>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Milestone">Notice to Proceed (NTP)</td><td data-label="Deadline / entry">One calendar month after Bidding Date.</td><td data-label="How to resolve">Record the actual <strong>Notice to Proceed</strong> date.</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Milestone">Material testing</td><td data-label="Deadline / entry">One calendar month after Bidding Date.</td><td data-label="How to resolve">Record <strong>Material Testing Date</strong>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Milestone">Final inspection</td><td data-label="Deadline / entry">Calculated Contract Due Date; when contract date/duration are absent, a saved Contract End Date is used.</td><td data-label="How to resolve">Record <strong>Final Inspection</strong>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Milestone">SWA follow-up</td><td data-label="Deadline / entry">One year after <strong>Completion Date</strong>, moved to a working date.</td><td data-label="How to resolve">Record <strong>Statement of Work Accomplished Date</strong>.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>Calculated due dates are read-only and do not fill actual dates. Calendar-month deadlines clamp to the last valid day of the next month, then move to the next working day if necessary. Admin controls reminder lead times; final-inspection reminders default to <strong>7 working days</strong> before the contract deadline. A valid actual milestone date on or before today resolves its alerts. Use actual dates only after the event happens. Do not enter a planned future date as Completion or SWA: the current system can immediately mark the project Completed or Released and hide its alerts.</p>
    <p>Status follows recorded milestones: no bidding date → <strong>On-going Bidding</strong>; bidding date → <strong>Pre-inspection</strong>; actual pre-inspection, material-testing and NTP dates all present → <strong>Pending</strong>. When a record is saved on or after its contract deadline, missing final inspection produces <strong>Final-inspection</strong>. Entering a valid <strong>Final Inspection Date</strong> sets the status to <strong>Pending</strong>, even before the contract deadline or when earlier milestone dates are missing. Completion Date produces <strong>Completed</strong>; SWA Date produces <strong>Released</strong>, which takes priority. A project explicitly kept Completed/Released retains that status. A Completed project requires a Completion Date and appears in Monthly Completions for that date’s month/year.</p>
    <p>Status colors: <strong>Pending—amber; On-going Bidding—blue; Pre-inspection—cyan; Final-inspection—purple; Completed—green; Released—teal.</strong> Read the label as well as its color. Completed projects can still need SWA follow-up until SWA is recorded.</p></div></details><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-6" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-6-title">Resolve and restore alerts</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><ol>
        <li>Choose <strong>Edit</strong> on the project, record the actual milestone date and save. Use <strong>Alerts</strong> in the project details or editor to check alert statuses and dates. NOA, pre-inspection, NTP, material-testing, final-inspection and SWA alerts resolve from their dates. Editing requires project-edit permission.</li>
        <li>Alerts resolve automatically from a valid actual milestone date on or before today, including older NOA and NTP reminders. A future date stays scheduled until that date. Recording or correcting a milestone requires <strong>Edit</strong> permission.</li>
        <li><strong>Resolved Alerts</strong> groups completed reminders by milestone. Use its search/date filters and category pages to review them. <strong>Restore</strong> reopens a historical manually resolved reminder and requires the <strong>Restore historical alerts</strong> permission. Automatically resolved entries offer <strong>View</strong>; edit or clear the actual date to reopen the reminder when due. Existing historical manual flags may also need restoring.</li>
    </ol></div></details></div></section><section id="projectUserGuideContent-task-files" class="help-task" data-help-task hidden aria-labelledby="projectUserGuideContent-task-files-title"><button type="button" class="help-back" data-help-home><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m14 5-7 7 7 7"/></svg><span>All topics</span></button><h2 id="projectUserGuideContent-task-files-title" tabindex="-1">Import, export &amp; print</h2><p class="help-task-description">Spreadsheets, printing and archives.</p><ol class="help-steps"><li>Choose <strong>Import</strong> and download the template, or select <strong>Export Excel</strong> for your current list.</li><li>For imports, check the preview and duplicate choices before saving.</li><li>Check the result. Open a project’s <strong>Print</strong> action when you need a reference copy.</li></ol><p class="help-note">If an import fails, check which rows were saved before retrying.</p><div class="help-more"><h3>More details</h3><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-9" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-9-title">Import, export, archive and deletion</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><ol>
        <li>With Import permission, choose <strong>Import</strong> and <strong>Download template</strong>. Keep headings, use one project per row, <strong>YYYY-MM-DD</strong> working dates and non-negative amounts with at most two decimals. Choose a CSV or Excel file.</li>
        <li>Review and edit the preview, scrolling horizontally for all columns. Correct invalid rows; invalid rows are skipped. For each duplicate, choose <strong>Add as a new project</strong> or <strong>Overwrite existing project</strong>; review bulk choices carefully. Choose <strong>Import reviewed rows</strong> and wait for the progress result.</li>
        <li>Review imported/skipped counts and any errors. If an import fails, check which records were already saved before retrying. Rollback is currently refused for batches that created projects, and later edits can also block an undo. Ask Admin to review affected records; do not assume an error means nothing was saved.</li>
        <li><strong>Export Excel</strong> downloads all records matching the current lifecycle and filters, across all pages. Check the view and filters before exporting; use Historical Archive to export archived records.</li>
        <li><strong>Archive</strong> keeps a project and its history for reference and removes it from the active dashboard/alerts. View it in <strong>Historical Archive</strong>; use <strong>Restore</strong> with archive permission to return it.</li>
        <li>The project row keeps <strong>Archive/Restore, Logs</strong> and the <strong>red trash-can icon</strong> on one line. Archive keeps a project for later restoration; the trash-can icon submits a Staff deletion request or opens the Admin’s direct deletion review. See <strong>Deletion requests &amp; approval</strong> for the required review and final confirmation.</li>
    </ol></div></details><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-7" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-7-title">Details, print and project Logs</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><ol><li>Select a project title to open <strong>Project Details</strong>. Review its amounts, milestone dates, remarks, attachments and Alerts. Viewing does not mark you as an editor.</li><li>Choose the row’s <strong>Logs</strong> button for the project’s saved snapshots, archive/restore events and timeline actions. Expand an entry to read the details. The author’s name and username appear when recorded; older entries may show <strong>Not recorded</strong>.</li><li>Choose <strong>Print</strong> in the project details and use the browser’s Print or Save as PDF option. Check the preview and selected paper settings. These are reference summaries.</li><li>Keep the original spreadsheet until an import has been checked: spreadsheet overwrites are not currently guaranteed to appear in per-project Logs. Contact IT if you need a complete change investigation.</li></ol><p><strong>Working dates:</strong> The shared calendar controls durations, reminder lead times and selectable dates. Saturdays, Sundays and excluded holidays are non-working by default. Ask IT about calendar corrections; Superadmin’s guide explains the calendar controls.</p></div></details></div></section><section id="projectUserGuideContent-task-deletion" class="help-task" data-help-task hidden aria-labelledby="projectUserGuideContent-task-deletion-title"><button type="button" class="help-back" data-help-home><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m14 5-7 7 7 7"/></svg><span>All topics</span></button><h2 id="projectUserGuideContent-task-deletion-title" tabindex="-1">Delete &amp; clear history</h2><p class="help-task-description">Requests, approvals and personal history.</p><ol class="help-steps" data-help-roles="staff"><li>Select the project’s <strong>red trash icon</strong>.</li><li>Enter a reason and choose <strong>Submit request</strong>.</li><li>Track the result in <strong>Deletion requests</strong>. The project stays until Admin confirms deletion.</li></ol><ol class="help-steps" data-help-roles="admin"><li>Select the project’s <strong>red trash icon</strong>, or open a Staff request.</li><li>Review the records and choose <strong>Continue to final confirmation</strong>.</li><li>Tick the confirmation box, then select <strong>Confirm deletion</strong>.</li></ol><p class="help-note"><strong>History → Clear history</strong> clears your view. It does not delete projects or other users’ request history.</p><div class="help-more"><h3>More details</h3><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-10" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-10-title">Deletion and two-step Admin verification</summary><div class="help-reference-body">
    <p>Staff submit deletion requests for Admin approval. Admin can delete directly after reviewing the records and confirming deletion on a second screen. Records stay intact until final confirmation.</p>
    <h3 class="h6">Delete directly as Admin</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Select the <strong>bold red trash-can icon</strong> beside a project. Its Admin tooltip is <strong>Delete project</strong>. Review the project and the included history and attachments. You may add an optional deletion note for the activity log.</li>
        <li>Choose the red <strong>Continue to final confirmation</strong> button. On the next screen, tick the confirmation checkbox and choose <strong>Confirm deletion</strong>. Only this final action deletes the records. Admin does not submit a request or wait for approval.</li>
        <li>Choose <strong>Cancel</strong>, <strong>Go back</strong>, or close the dialog before final confirmation to keep the records. No pending request is created. Confirmation expires after ten minutes, and changed records must be reviewed again.</li>
        <li>If a Staff request already covers the project, the trash can opens that request for review instead. For <strong>Delete all records</strong>, review the selected records and complete the same two steps.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3 class="h6">Submit a request as Staff</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>In <strong>View All Projects</strong> or <strong>Historical Archive</strong>, select the <strong>bold red trash-can icon</strong> beside Archive/Restore and Logs. Its tooltip is <strong>Request deletion</strong>. The icon is available when your account has the request-deletion permission.</li>
        <li>Enter the reason and choose <strong>Submit request</strong>. Submitting the request does not delete the record.</li>
        <li>Open <strong>Deletion requests</strong> in the sidebar to check the result. For Staff, <strong>Active</strong> shows requests awaiting review, and approved or closed requests move to <strong>History</strong>. Open <strong>View request</strong> for the reason, included records, decision note and timestamps. Staff see only their own requests. In <strong>History</strong>, choose <strong>Clear history</strong> to clear all outcomes and pages from your view. This affects only your account; active requests, other users’ history and the saved request records remain available. For Admin, this workspace button opens the approval queue for submitted requests. Its badge counts requests awaiting review or final confirmation; direct Admin deletion does not add a pending request.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3 class="h6">Clear request history</h3><p>Open <strong>History → Clear history</strong> and confirm. This clears all outcomes and pages from your own view, including outcomes hidden by a filter. Other users’ history and the saved request records remain available. The Admin’s pending and approved queue stays active. A Staff request already approved may be in personal History even while Admin is still awaiting final confirmation. New closed requests appear normally afterward.</p><h3 class="h6">Edit or cancel your pending request</h3>
    <ol><li>Press the project’s red trash can again to reopen your pending request instead of submitting another one. A pending bulk request opens when it includes that project.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Edit reason</strong>, change the text and select <strong>Save reason</strong>. If the request was already approved, changing its reason resets that approval and sends it back for a fresh review.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Cancel request</strong> and confirm to withdraw it. The project, history and attachments remain intact. Cancelled requests stay in your request history and can be filtered by <strong>Cancelled</strong>.</li></ol>
    <h3 class="h6">Review Staff requests as Admin</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Open <strong>Workspace → Deletion requests</strong>, then choose <strong>Review request</strong>. Check the requester, reason and included records. Add an optional Admin note.</li>
        <li>Choose the red <strong>Continue to final confirmation</strong> button to approve the request and open the final-confirmation dialog. The same button is used for requests already approved. <strong>Reject request</strong> declines the request and keeps the project.</li>
        <li>Review the final-confirmation dialog, tick the checkbox and select <strong>Confirm deletion</strong>. Only this final action removes the approved project, its history and its attachments.</li>
        <li>Choose <strong>Go back</strong> or close the dialog to stop before deletion. The request stays Approved and awaits final confirmation. For Staff it appears in <strong>History</strong>; Admin keeps it in the workspace’s Active approval queue until finished or withdrawn.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="table-responsive"><table class="table table-sm">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request status</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td data-label="Request status">Pending</td><td data-label="What it means">Awaiting Admin review and visible in Active. The records remain intact.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Request status">Approved</td><td data-label="What it means">Reviewed and awaiting final confirmation. It moves to personal History and stays in the Admin queue. The project remains intact until confirmation.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Request status">Rejected</td><td data-label="What it means">The Admin declined the request. Read the Admin note; the records remain intact.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Request status">Deleted</td><td data-label="What it means">An Admin completed both steps. The request retains who requested, reviewed and confirmed it, with the relevant dates.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Request status">Cancelled</td><td data-label="What it means">The requester withdrew the request. All records were kept.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p><strong>Bulk deletion:</strong> Staff with the separate permission can choose <strong>Request deletion of all records</strong> for Admin approval. Admin chooses <strong>Delete all records</strong> and completes direct review and final confirmation. Archives are included; projects added after the reviewed selection are excluded.</p>
    <p>If a project or its history changes before direct Admin confirmation, reopen deletion and review the current records again. For a Staff request, reject the outdated request and submit a fresh one. Staff can reopen a pending request to edit or cancel it; cancellation releases the records for a fresh request.</p>
</div></details></div></section><section id="projectUserGuideContent-task-account" class="help-task" data-help-task hidden aria-labelledby="projectUserGuideContent-task-account-title"><button type="button" class="help-back" data-help-home><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m14 5-7 7 7 7"/></svg><span>All topics</span></button><h2 id="projectUserGuideContent-task-account-title" tabindex="-1">Your account &amp; settings</h2><p class="help-task-description">Profile, access and office settings.</p><ol class="help-steps" data-help-roles="staff"><li>Open your <strong>top-right avatar → Edit profile</strong>.</li><li>Update your name or photo and save.</li><li>Choose <strong>Sign out</strong> when you finish using a shared computer.</li></ol><ol class="help-steps" data-help-roles="admin"><li>Open <strong>Admin</strong> for timeline settings, recent activity and backups.</li><li>Change the setting you need and check the saved confirmation.</li><li>Use your <strong>top-right avatar</strong> to edit your profile or sign out.</li></ol><p class="help-note">Contact IT (Superadmin) for accounts, password help or Staff permissions.</p><div class="help-more"><h3>More details</h3><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-13" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-13-title">Profile and sign out</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><p>Each account has one active browser session. Signing in on another browser or device signs out the previous session; tabs in the same browser can stay open. Admin and Staff are signed out after <strong>30 minutes without typing, clicking or scrolling</strong>. Background updates do not extend this timer. A warning appears one minute before expiry; choose <strong>Stay signed in</strong> to continue. Every session ends after eight hours. If a session ends while editing, sign in with the same account in the same tab to recover the draft. Do not refresh or close that tab before recovery; unsaved fields are kept only in that tab’s memory. Review restored changes before saving.</p><ol><li>Open your top-right avatar → <strong>Edit profile</strong> to change your display name or photo. Use a JPG, PNG or WebP up to 3 MB, position the crop and save. Choose <strong>Sign out</strong> from the same menu when finished.</li></ol>
    <div class="alert alert-light border mb-0"><strong>Need help?</strong> Contact IT for access, connection or calendar issues and your Admin for project questions. Include the project number, attempted action and displayed message. If a session expires, sign in again. Copy unsaved field changes before leaving the page.</div></div></details><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-1" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-1-title">Sign in, navigation and permissions</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><ol>
        <li>Open the tracker link and sign in with your own username and password. Contact IT (Superadmin) for a new account, password assistance or account permissions. Staff cannot register their own accounts.</li>
        <li>The sidebar opens <strong>Dashboard, View All Projects, Historical Archive, Resolved Alerts</strong> and <strong>Deletion requests</strong>. For Admin, <strong>Admin</strong> appears below Deletion requests. Choose <strong>Add Project</strong> from the project view when you have permission. On smaller screens, open the navigation menu to switch pages.</li>
        <li><strong>Admin</strong> can review deletion requests, confirm final deletion, and manage project operations, timeline settings, recent activity and backups. Only Superadmin can create and manage accounts. <strong>Staff</strong> can view records, details, logs, alerts, attachments and printable summaries. Superadmin separately grants Add, Edit, Import, Export, Request deletion, Request deletion of all records, Restore historical alerts and Archive/restore. Deletion permission lets Staff request deletion; an Admin must approve and confirm it.</li>
    </ol></div></details><details id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-12" class="help-reference" data-guide-topic data-help-roles="admin"><summary id="projectUserGuideContent-topic-12-title">Admin operations</summary><div class="help-reference-body"><ol>
        <li><strong>Admin → Timeline day settings</strong>: choose standard durations or <strong>Custom</strong> values from 1–3,650 working days, then <strong>Save timeline days</strong>. Settings cover NOA, shared pre-inspection/NTP/material reminders, SWA and final inspection. Reminder settings change when alerts appear; the bidding-based deadlines remain one calendar month after bidding.</li>
        <li><strong>Accounts:</strong> only IT (Superadmin) can create or manage accounts, including Staff and Admin accounts. Contact IT for account creation, password assistance or Staff permissions. Admin has no account-creation form.</li>
        <li><strong>Recent activity → Refresh</strong> reloads recorded actions. <strong>Clear history</strong> requires confirmation and clears the visible recent-activity list; older audit entries remain stored. This clears the shared recent-activity view for Admin accounts. This is separate from an individual project’s Audit Trail.</li>
        <li><strong>Automatic project backups</strong>: set the destination using <strong>Browse</strong>, <strong>Use default</strong> or the path field; use the On/Off control to save the preference. <strong>Back up projects now</strong> creates a manual archive. Check its result and latest-backup details. Scheduled daily/weekly/monthly copies need the server scheduler configured by IT.</li>
        <li>Project backups include project records, project history, numbering, an Excel export and attachments. They currently omit deletion requests and approval decisions, general activity, accounts/passwords, profile photos and settings. Ask IT for a separate full-system backup and restoration test.</li>
    </ol></div></details></div></section></div>
